# What a critical rate over 100% is good for: at max level, half of it comes
# back as critical damage. 20 + x% of the rate: 21% at level 1 and 50% at 30, so
# an archer at 120% gets 60% critical damage.
#
# Critical rate a swing states for itself doesn't count, as GMS says outright:
# Snipe's guaranteed critical doesn't add. The engine already splits character
# and swing, so the lever reads the character's.
#
# The roll still caps at 100%; the excess is used here and nowhere else, as GMS
# also says.
name: "Vicious Shot"
description:
  "When inflicting a critical wound, your strike hits the enemy where they "
  "are most vulnerable, dealing greater damage."
kind: SKILL_KIND_ACTIVE
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_BOW_MASTER_V skill_order: 13 }
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_MARKSMAN_V skill_order: 7 }
v_node: V_NODE_KIND_ARCHETYPE
max_level: 30
base_delay_ms: 120
cooldown_seconds: 120.0
buff {
  duration_seconds: 30.0
  base { crit_dmg_per_crit_rate: 0.21 }
  per_level { crit_dmg_per_crit_rate: 0.01 }
}
